hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"288","\nNarrated to us Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Makhzūmī and ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn al-ʿAlāʾ, who said:\nSufyān narrated to us. ʿAbd al-Jabbār said: Manṣūr narrated to us, and Saʿīd said: from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, from Hammām.\n\nAnd narrated to us Abū Hāshim Ziyād ibn Ayyūb: Ziyād ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Bakkāʾī narrated to us: Manṣūr narrated to us, from Ibrāhīm, from Hammām.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Kurayb: Abū Usāmah narrated to us.\n\nAnd narrated to us ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd al-Ashajj: Ibn Numayr narrated to us.\n\nAnd narrated to us Bundār: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us.\n\nAll of them narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from Hammām.\n\nAnd narrated to us ʿAlī ibn Khashram: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus informed us, from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from Hammām.\n\nAnd narrated to us Naṣr ibn Marzūq al-Miṣrī: Asad ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from al-Ḥakam, from Ibrāhīm, from Hammām ibn al-Ḥārith.\n\nAnd narrated to us Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā ibn Zayd al-Lakhmī al-Tinnīsī: ʿAmr ibn Abī Salamah narrated to us, from al-Awzāʿī, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī, from al-Qāsim.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd al-Qurashī: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us: Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us, from Abū Maʿshar, from al-Nakhaʿī, from al-Aswad ibn Yazīd.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd: Yaʿlā narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated to us, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā: Yaʿlā narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated to us, from Ibrāhīm, from Hammām.\n\nAnd narrated to us ʿAbd al-Wārith ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad: my father narrated to me: Mahdī ibn Maymūn narrated to us, from Wāṣil, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā: Musaddad narrated to us: Abū ʿAwānah narrated to us, from al-Mughīrah ibn Miqsam and Ḥammād ibn Abī Sulaymān, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā: al-Khaḍir ibn Muḥammad ibn Shujāʿ and Ibn al-Ṭabbāʿ narrated to us: they both said: Hāshim informed us: al-Mughīrah narrated to us, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ḥammād ibn Abī Sulaymān, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad.\n\nAnd narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Ḥakīm: Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿAdī narrated to us, from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah.\n\nAnd narrated to us Hārūn ibn Isḥāq al-Hamdānī: ʿAbdah narrated to us, from Saʿīd, from Abū Maʿshar, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad.\n\nAnd narrated to us Abū Bishr al-Wāsiṭī: Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ, from Abū Maʿshar, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah and al-Aswad.\n\nAnd narrated to us Naṣr ibn Marzūq: Asad narrated to us: al-Masʿūdī narrated to us, from al-Ḥakam and Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from Hammām ibn al-Ḥārith.\n\nAnd narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Ḥakīm: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: al-Masʿūdī narrated to us, from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from Hammām ibn al-Ḥārith.\n\nAnd narrated to us Bashar ibn Muʿādh al-ʿAqadī: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us.\nAnd narrated to us Abū Hāshim al-Rummānī: from Abū Majlaz Lāhiq ibn Ḥumayd, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Nawfal.\n\nAnd narrated to us Naṣr ibn Marzūq al-Miṣrī: Asad ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Qazaʿah ibn Suwayd narrated to us: Ḥumayd al-Aʿraj and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Najīḥ narrated to us, from Mujāhid.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā: Hāniʾ ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Qazaʿah narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ and Ḥumayd al-Aʿraj, from Mujāhid.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Qazaʿah ibn Suwayd narrated to us: Ḥumayd narrated to us, from Mujāhid.\n\nAnd narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Ḥakīm: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us.\nAnd narrated to us ʿAbbād ibn Manṣūr: al-Qāsim narrated to us.\n\nAnd narrated to us ʿAlī ibn Sahl al-Ramlī: Zayd ibn Abī al-Zarqāʾ narrated to us, from Jaʿfar ibn Burqān, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā: Ḥusn ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us: Shabīb ibn Gharqadah narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shihāb al-Khawlānī.\n\nAll of these narrators narrated from ʿĀʾishah (RA), who said:\n*\She used to scrape off the semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\""*\nSome of them abbreviated the hadith"","" while others mentioned the descent of a guest upon her and the washing of her blanket. She also said:\n*\""I have seen myself scraping it from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\""*"""""
"289","Our father Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Yahya bin Salamah bin Kuhail, my father told me, on the authority of his father Salamah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I used to remove ritual impurity from the garment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a pebble.”"
"290","On the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ishaq, meaning the blue one, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qais, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Aisha, “She was under Semen from the garment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying.”"
